# The topic branches `integration` carries, merged onto upstream nolabs-ai/nono `main` in this
# order by .github/integration/rebuild. One per line: the branch, then what it fixes (Markdown,
# copied into INTEGRATION.md). Each branch is based on upstream `main`.
#
# A branch here that is missing or does not merge stops the rebuild: nothing is pushed or built,
# and an issue stays open until a rebuild succeeds. Drop a line when its fix lands upstream.
#
# A PR that changes this file is a carry PR, under the fork's rules (AGENTS.md here): upstream's
# NEP, DCO sign-off and disclosure apply when a topic is submitted upstream, not to a carry.
#
# Not carried:
#   fix/credential-capture-owned-children  superseded by nolabs-ai/nono#2073, which fixes
#     nolabs-ai/nono#1620 and also covers supervisor credential sources (the branch is kept)
#   fix/claude-securestorage-config-dir  superseded by nolabs-ai/nono#2085, which fixes
#     nolabs-ai/nono#1950 the same way and also matches the preflight Keychain lookup to it
#     (the branch is kept)

fix/supervisor-audit-rate-limited-capability-requests  Remainder of nolabs-ai/nono#2043 after #2047: capability requests refused by the approval rate limiter left no audit record
fix/drain-command-proxy-audit  Follow-up to nolabs-ai/nono#1981: command-scoped proxy audit events were never drained into the session audit record
fix/profile-show-sandbox-policy  `nono profile show` / `profile diff` omitted `linux.sandbox_policy` in text and JSON
metadata-ops-confine  nolabs-ai/nono#914: Landlock does not mediate chmod/utime; `linux.metadata_mediation = "write_grants"` confines them to write grants
feat/proxy-resolved-address-classes  `network.resolved_addresses`: with `public_only`, an allowed name that resolves to a loopback, private or shared (CGNAT) address is refused unless an exception names that class for it, and one that resolves to an unspecified address is refused with no exception possible (a link-local one is refused in any case) (upstream draft not filed)
